TEXT -800 -624 Left 5 ;In this example the generator is loaded with P=3000W Q=1500W\nGenerator is overexited (produce P=-3000W, Q=-1500W) \nThe .plt files with appended 1,2,3,4 shows \nisx, isy, usx, usy, theta, is, us for all four cases (multiplied by drawing factor)\nFor the drawings of the four cases see diagram1.png in this folder
TEXT -224 -352 Left 2 ;Reduced Roff to 1e6 for better convergence
TEXT 200 -616 Left 5 ;Drawing the diagram:\n=================\n \nThe drawing nr. 1 shows the generator with normal speed\n=============================================\nFirst draw Us at the positive r-axis\nSecond draw the q-line with angle theta2 = theta=7.7degrees \nThird draw the d-line \nThe d-line is always negative at +i\nThe speed direction is normal so it is clockwise\nSpeed direction is always from +q to +d therefore you can now set also the direction of the q-axis\nNow you can draw ud, uq, id, iq \nHINT: Although the speed direction can change the reference direction of omega*t is always counterclockwise (from +r to +i)\nsince t is always positive in the transient simulation !\nTherefore you can see that IN in all four cases is leading Us which should be so for a overexcited generator\nYou can also see that the output power is in all four cases S=-P-jQ (which is so in loadreference arrow system)\nTEST it by setting the magnitude of U,I=1 for U and I : S=U*conj(I)=1*(-1-1j)=-1-1j  \nIn the examples 3,4 the magnitude of U=-1\n \nThe drawing nr. 2 shows the generator with reverse speed\n===============================================\nFirst draw Us at the positive r-axis\nSecond draw the q-line with angle theta2 = 180-theta=7.7degrees \nThird draw the d-line \nThe speed direction is reversed so it is counterclockwise\nSpeed direction is always from +q to +d therefore you can now set also the direction of the q-axis\nNow you can draw ud, uq, id, iq \n \nThe drawing nr. 3 shows the generator with normal speed and negative magnetic voltage\n======================================================================\nFirst draw Us at the negative r-axis\nSecond draw the q-line with angle theta2 = 180+theta=7.7degrees \nThird draw the d-line \nThe speed direction is normal so it is rclockwise\nSpeed direction is always from +q to +d therefore you can now set also the direction of the q-axis\nNow you can draw ud, uq, id, iq \n \nThe drawing nr. 4 shows the generator with reverse speed and negative magnetic voltage\n=======================================================================\nFirst draw Us at the negative r-axis\nSecond draw the q-line with angle theta2 = -theta=7.7degrees \nThird draw the d-line \nThe speed direction is reversed so it is counterclockwise\nSpeed direction is always from +q to +d therefore you can now set also the direction of the q-axis\nNow you can draw ud, uq, id, iq
